# LF in the repository, whatever the checkout does locally.
#
# This project was written on Windows and now builds on macOS too. Without this,
# every file committed from Windows carries CRLF, and a macOS checkout either sees
# the whole tree as modified or quietly rewrites it back — which turns any real diff
# into noise. Shell scripts and the Electron entry points genuinely need LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only helpers, which cmd and PowerShell are happier reading as CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.wasm binary
